 A later act copying the registry without re-attesting the row cannot have absorbed an unattested change to its approved cells, only to its routed traced cells, so the first arm proves the copy is the re-attesting act's own and the second proves the row's routed traced cells are the same at the range's two ends, whether the range is one squashed commit or many. The second arm's one limit: a routed traced cell moved before the re-attesting act and restored after it is re-anchored by a later act's copy of the registry, as any traced refresh is, and the row settles. A row re-attested in the range whose routed traced cells moved in the range is not proven settled when a later act copies its registry, so it is minted even when its own act judged it. The comparison includes cells outside the net range diff. A tree that does not list the ledger supplies no acts, and a missing copy or a copy without the row leaves the record to mint. A listed ledger or snapshot copy that cannot be read or does not parse refuses the mint by naming the carrier and revision; it is never treated as absent. The same filtering result serves the post-merge and range-sweep routes. Its refusal states that the mint was refused while the merge stands and directs recovery through a fetch followed by a sweep over the same range, or through a reviewed repair followed by a sweep whose after revision is the repairing commit. The contract covers ledger and snapshot inputs produced by supported signing and act routes; hand-edited carriers, alias spellings and sub-second timing windows are outside it.\""," rationale = \"Suppressing a record without both a new re-attestation and equality to its approved copy would hide a later amendment; treating a present unreadable carrier as absence would make the suppression decision unauditable. The later-writer arm accepts one bound rather than minting on every later copy of the registry: a routed traced cell restored between two acts is re-anchored by the later copy, as the snapshot already re-anchors any traced change without a verdict.\""," test_refs = \"(see TC-403)\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"," "]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-963\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1540,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1540,"newLines":7,"lines":[" expected = \"Satisfies SR-178 AcceptanceCriteria through the LLR-364 filtering contract, both arms of its later-writer condition and the second arm's stated limit included over squashed and unsquashed ranges, and IF-091 call outcome.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_row_reattested_in_range_and_equal_to_its_copy_mints_nothing; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_row_amended_again_after_its_act_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_an_amendment_with_no_act_in_range_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_an_absent_ledger_filters_nothing; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_the_filter_is_not_consulted_without_amendment_records; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_malformed_ledger_refuses_the_mint_by_name; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_an_unreadable_ledger_blob_refuses_the_mint_by_name; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_malformed_snapshot_copy_refuses_the_mint_by_name; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_an_unreadable_snapshot_copy_blob_refuses_the_mint_by_name; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_reattested_row_missing_from_its_copy_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_cell_restored_after_the_act_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_routed_traced_cell_moved_after_the_act_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_an_unrouted_traced_cell_moved_after_the_act_still_settles; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_later_act_copying_the_registry_does_not_settle_a_row_it_did_not_reattest; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_later_act_copying_another_registry_leaves_the_row_settled; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_later_legacy_act_leaves_the_row_unsettled; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_later_writer_leaves_a_row_with_unmoved_routed_cells_settled; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_later_writer_leaves_a_row_with_moved_routed_cells_unsettled; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_routed_cell_restored_between_two_acts_copying_the_registry_settles; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_a_routed_cell_restored_after_the_act_with_no_later_copy_still_mints; tests/test_intake_settled.py::test_the_two_real_redundant_landings_mint_nothing\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-154]"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-963\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-963\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019UHGGioxk9nJRUyDGd2afZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
